Index: Project

Purpose:
  Project model registry and routing table. This file defines the SHAPE
  of how projects are structured — the Project > Domain > Module > Feature
  > Component hierarchy — and routes to model files.

  This folder contains MODEL and SCHEMA only — no concrete project data.
  Concrete project instances live under .sdd/projects/<name>/.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1  project.sdd   (project model entry point)
   2  INDEX.sdd     (this file — project model map)
   3  domains.sdd   (domain schema and list)
   4  modules.sdd   (module schema and list)
   5  map.sdd       (project navigation map)
   6  flows.sdd     (execution flow schema)
   7  dependencies.sdd (dependency schema)
   8  indexes.sdd   (category-level index schema)
   9  instantiation.sdd (project instantiation rules)
   10 mode.sdd      (project mode schema)
   11 architecture.sdd (architecture schema)
   12 README.sdd    (project model overview)

Rules:
  [PM1] This folder defines reusable project structure schemas only.
  [PM2] Concrete project instances MUST live under .sdd/projects/<name>/.
  [PM3] AI MUST NOT place project state (decisions, tasks, docs, etc.)
        in this folder — use .sdd/projects/<name>/ instead.
  [PM4] Domain and module schemas defined here are templates; concrete
        instances belong to the instantiated project.

Navigation:
  ProjectModel: @project.sdd
  Domains: @domains.sdd
  Modules: @modules.sdd
  Map: @map.sdd
  Flows: @flows.sdd
  Dependencies: @dependencies.sdd
  Indexes: @indexes.sdd
  Instantiation: @instantiation.sdd
  Mode: @mode.sdd
  Architecture: @architecture.sdd
  Readme: @README.sdd
  Projects: @../projects/INDEX.sdd
  ProjectInstances: @../projects/
  Root: @../INDEX.sdd

State: +
  (converted to model-only registry; concrete instances moved to projects/<name>/)
